Description: Debian on Synology NAS (DS920+, DS923+): hardware support
 The platform drivers (bay power with DSM-style staggered spin-up and hot-plug,
 USB VBUS, fan hwmon, disk LEDs, S-35390A RTC) are built into the synodeb
 kernel (linux-image-synodeb-longterm or linux-image-synodeb-stable). This
 package was called synology-ds923 until version 3.5. It adds synohwd, the daemon for the
 front-panel microcontroller (fans, LEDs, buttons, beeper, power-on after an
 AC loss, scheduled power-on), udev and systemd configuration, the hardware
 watchdog, the DSM NVMe power limit, synodeb-dom (kernel and boot entries on
 the Synology DOM, with automatic fallback to the previous kernel),
 notifications (e-mail, Telegram, ntfy) for SMART, RAID, fans, shutdowns and
 failed units, UPS support with NUT and a DSM-like Safe Mode (synodeb-ups),
 and synodeb-dsm to read DSM data volumes read-only.

